WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.169
-Tonight's guest is a
Golden Globe nominated actress

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.870
and Grammy-winning
country music star.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.740
She stars in
"Big Sky: Deadly Trails,"

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.809
which premieres September 21st
on ABC.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.910
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.680
-How's it look?
-Well, it's crooked, hon.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.748
Pull it up on the right
just a little bit.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.083
-That's good enough.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.885
-Now, Buck, these people
paid good money

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:21.821
for a luxury back-country
experience.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.789
The least you could do
is hang the damn sign straight.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.092
-Well, I --
-This is a new site for us, hon.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.760
We gotta make it shine.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.328
-[Quietly] I'm aware of that.
-What was that?

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:30.797
-Uh, I love you, dear.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:34.300
-Please welcome back to the
show, Reba McEntire, everybody!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.403
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:41.774 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:46.112 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:50.516 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.750
-Thank you so much!

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.952
Thank you!

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.320
Alright!

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.354
Nice.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.689
-So happy to have you here,
Reba!

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.690
How are you doing?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.958
-I'm doing great.
Good to be here.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.326
-It's great to have you.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.863
You play the questionable owner
of a glamping site

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.331
on this show, and I'm wondering

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.933
if you have done any glamping in
real life.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.068
-Absolutely not.
-What about camping?

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.403
-No. No.
-Any camping?

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.704
Okay, why not?

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.172
Not even growing up,
you never went camping?

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.809
-No. My idea of camping is
Holiday Inn.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.010
-Okay.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.077
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.179
-How many agree with me?

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.947
[ Cheering ]

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:23.983
That's what I thought.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.019
-Now, to be fair, that probably,
to some degree,

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:28.721
is because you did grow up
on a ranch,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:32.092
and so the allure of camping
probably had...yeah.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.759
I get it.
-No, we were up in the hills,

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.461
gathering cattle,
working cattle.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:38.197
I got lost several times,
me and my little sister Susie.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:41.434
Alice and Pake knew where they
were going, we never did.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.704
It was 8,000 acres,
so we got lost.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.238
-Right.
-So I wanted to be home.

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:49.075
-Yeah. So you would
accidentally go camping.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.144
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.613
-Unplanned.
-Unplanned camping.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.882
You have said, and this does
make sense to me,

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:58.250
growing up on a ranch helped you

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.821
both as a musician
and as an actor,

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.790
because you have to take
a lot of direction on a ranch.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.459
What kind of direction
are you receiving?

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:10.396
-If, when we leave --
this is Daddy talking --

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.998
"Alright, we're gonna take these

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.599
150 head of cattle
along down there.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:14.934
You sit in that gate
and make sure

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.169
nobody gets around
and gets back up in the hills."

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.904
And you heard about
a fourth of that.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:21.274
So you're going,
"Yes, sir. Yes, sir. Yes, sir."

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.876
Then he'd ride off and I'd say,
"Grandpap, what did he say?"

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.445
"He said sit in the gate."
I said, "Okay."

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.813
[ Laughter ]
-There you go.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.814
-And you better be in that gate
when Daddy gets back.

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.783
-So you could take
direction well.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.219
We actually have a blooper reel
from your show, "Reba,"

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.087
where you are receiving
direction.

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.189
-Oh, no.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:40.092
-Because it seems that
everyone involved

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:43.262
thinks that your pronunciation
of the word "ice"

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.231
sounds a little bit too much
like "ass."

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.499
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.499 --> 00:02:50.269
-Even on my phone,
when I dictate a message,

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:51.371
it does that.
-Really?

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.638
-Yes.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:55.040
I say "iced tea,"
it goes "ass tea."

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.210
I'm like, "I did not say that."

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:02.348
-Don't accidentally ever order
on Amazon by voice, you know?

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.351
You never want the ass tea
to show up.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.020
Let's take a look at
this reel real quick.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.021
-Okay.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.389
[Heavily accented ] Chewing ice.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.024
Chewing ice.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.825
Chewing ice.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.560
-[ Laughs ]
-Ice.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.529
[ Man shouting off seat ]
-Ice!

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.764
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:21.200
-Even the judge thought
that was funny.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.835
-Even the judge, yeah.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.671
I have to ask about a cameo
you did

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:27.773
in one of my favorite films
from the last couple years,

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:30.075
called "Barb and Star go to
Vista Del Mar."

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:31.811
[ Cheering ]
-Thank you!

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:34.981
-And you played -- you said,
was it a water sprite?

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.749
What did they say?

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.317
-Water spirit.
-A water spirit, excuse me.

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:42.388
-Not a Sprite. Not like
a water Coke or a water 7-Up.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.656
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.157
-Excuse me, it's a water spirit.

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:46.992
And now, how do you...

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:49.628
When you get a call, how do they
explain it to you,

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:50.630
what you're being offered?

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.898
-Well, I was just like you.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:54.133
When they said, "You're gonna be
playing a water spirit,"

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.201
and I said, "Like a mermaid?"

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.369
"No."

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.904
"Then what's a water spirit?"

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.939
"Kind of like a mer--"
"See? A mermaid."

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.307
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.742
-I think mermaid's pretty close
to what you are.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.910
-I do, too.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.577
-And you just showed up
for a couple days,

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.380
jumped in the water,
and knocked it out, right?

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.882
-Yeah, yeah. It was in the bay
there in Cancun.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.985
-Wow, so that's not a bad way
to a couple days' work.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:14.720
-Heck no. Loved it.
Had a lot of fun.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.122
-Yeah, well, they're very fun.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.790
-Annie and Kristen are pretty
fun people.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.359
-We got to go out
and eat dinner with them.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.694
And they had just come
from Mexico City,

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.028
where they got food poisoning.

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.696
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God.

00:04:24.696 --> 00:04:27.333
So they told us all that story.
They're hysterical.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.735
-That's a fun story to hear
at dinner.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.470
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.172
-I didn't think about that.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.774
-Hey, this is really cool.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.909
I guess it's
the 45th anniversary

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.744
of the first time you played
the Grand Ole Opry.

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:40.179
-It is.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.214
-What are your memories
of that night?

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.450
-Mom and Daddy
and my sister Alice

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:49.121
drove 650-700 miles
from Oklahoma to be with me

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:50.990
at my debut at
the Grand Ole Opry.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.626
'Cause we'd been going there
forever, all my life.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.596
Matter of fact, that's about
the only vacation we took,

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.230
was to Nashville to see
the Grand Ole Opry

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.632
at the Ryman Auditorium.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:03.936
So when we pulled up to the back
entrance of Grand Ole Opry,

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.371
Daddy rolled down his window.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.606
The gentleman stepped up
with his clipboard,

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:11.210
and Daddy said, "Reba McEntire,
performing on the show tonight."

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.345
And that guy went --

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:15.380
"Not tonight."

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.683
My heart stopped,
and Daddy said,

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.051
"Well, feller, what do you think
we ought to do?"

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.452
And he said,
"Well, I suggest you go home."

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:21.487
He said,
"Well, we can't do that.

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:24.089
We drove 700 miles to get here."

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:26.992
So I said, "Daddy, let's go
across the interstate

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:29.095
to the Get-and-Go,
and I'll call my agent."

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.831
So I did, and he said,
"You just go right back there."

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.999
We pulled up again
and the guy said,

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.735
"Right over there.
Number 28, Mr. McEntire.

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:37.837
So glad y'all are here."

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.772
-Wow.
-And then,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.308
I got inside and got my
little outfit on,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.043
and they came up to me and said,

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:47.046
"Reba, we're gonna have to take
one of your songs tonight."

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.315
I said, "I only get to do one?"
They said, "Yeah."

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.750
I said, "Why?"

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.218
They said, "Well, Dolly Parton
just pulled in parking lot,

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:55.154
and we're gonna give her
one of your songs."

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.856
I said, "Shoot, she can have
both of them."

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.958
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.694
-Wow, so the first night,
Dolly was in the building

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:02.828
the same night you did
your first performance

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:03.829
at the Grand Ole Opry.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.231
That's really something.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.833
-How about that? And you're back
on tour this year as well.

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:08.867
-I am.
-Is that exciting?

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:10.202
-Oh, my gosh. We're so excited.

00:06:10.202 --> 00:06:13.405
We went January-February-March
touring,

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:16.642
and we hadn't toured in 2 years,
and that's the first time --

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.678
I just don't know when the last
time was that I had 2 years off.

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:21.480
Ever. Never.
-Wow.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:27.320
-And so we had it ready
to go out on tour January 2020.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.256
COVID hit, and so we've been
sitting around

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.458
waiting for the opportunity
to go back out.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.594
We got to do January this year
and had a blast.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.829
And the crowds were magnificent.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.897
-Yeah, so they're still grateful
to be out again?

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:42.001
-They were so ready
to hear live music,

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:44.971
and boy, we gave our best shows,
worked our hardest.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.072
-Well, I would expect
nothing less.

00:06:47.072 --> 00:06:49.007
It's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:50.542
Thanks so much for
making time for us tonight.

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.211
-My pleasure.
-Reba McEntire!

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.979
"Big Sky: Deadly Trails"

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:55.848
premieres September 21st
on ABC.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.583
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

